# My Workspace

This authenticated, web-only domain is included by default in compatible Angular monolith prints.
The host registers its lazy route and sidebar link from `domain.json`; no platform route or navigation
registration is part of this folder.

The UI calls the REST Workspace Tasks API through `@forge/ui-contracts/v1`. Its configured
`apiPath` is `/api/v1/workspace/tasks`; the platform joins that path with the public `apiUrl`,
removing only overlapping boundary path segments. This supports an origin-only API URL, a URL
already ending in `/api` or `/api/v1`, and API URLs with other path prefixes. The platform supplies
the runtime API origin and bearer authentication. Do not copy tokens, host imports, or tenant/user
selectors into this domain.

The generated REST API must separately include Workspace Tasks and its PostgreSQL migration. The
Tasks screen never uses mock data and never falls back to it. See the generated REST print's
Workspace Tasks reference for the API contract, ownership rules, and deployment/migration
prerequisites.

## Workspaces CRUDA reference screen (mock data)

`/workspace/workspaces` is the reusable list/create/read/update/delete reference screen for future
domain modules. It is UI-first: no Workspaces API, database or AWS resource exists yet. Records,
Members, the Audit timeline, export and restore are all simulated in the browser and are labelled
"mock" in the UI.

- The data source is chosen only by the public option `workspaceRecordsMode` in
  `domain.config.json`. `mock` selects the in-browser mock. Any other value selects a source that
  fails visibly with a reference code. Mock data is never a fallback for API or authentication errors.
- Screens talk to the `WorkspaceRecordsData` port (`workspaces/sources`). A live implementation
  replaces the mock by providing that port; components and state do not change.
- Everything lives under `workspaces/`: contracts, constants, data, route-scoped Signals state,
  components (AG Grid Community grid, drawer, form, detail, delete dialog) and the page. It uses
  PrimeNG, AG Grid Community, the shared `--color-*` theme tokens and `@forge/ui-contracts/v1` only.
- To reuse the pattern, copy `workspaces/`, rename the record types, columns and copy, and register a
  route that calls `provideWorkspaceRecords()` (rename it to match your module).

The domain owns its request/response contracts, API client, route-scoped Signals state, task editor,
tests, and these usage notes. It uses only relative URLs and public V1 contracts so the complete
`workspace` folder can be copied unchanged into another compatible print.
